    "body": "# What does this PR do ?\n\nFixes `L2_Launch_models_exaone` on H100 and GB200, which has failed on `main` since #6401 (first failing nightly: [run 38987004275](https://github.com/NVIDIA-NeMo/Megatron-Bridge/actions/runs/38987004275) on 20dd692f1).\n\n```\nAssertionError: Converted provider for exaone4-config-only is missing attributes: {'rope_scaling_original_max_position_embeddings', 'rope_scaling_low_freq_factor', 'rope_scaling_high_freq_factor'}\n```\n\n**Cause:** #6401 stopped setting `rope_scaling_low_freq_factor`, `rope_scaling_high_freq_factor` and `rope_scaling_original_max_position_embeddings` on the EXAONE 4.0 provider. They are not `TransformerConfig` fields, and Megatron Core's llama3 RoPE scaling hardcodes them to 1.0, 4.0 and 8192. The bridge now warns when an HF config asks for other values. `test_exaone4_provider.py` still set all three on its expected provider, and `compare_provider_configs` requires both providers to have the same attribute names. #6401 had no `full-test-suite` label, so this L2 test did not run on that PR.\n\n# Changelog\n\n- Remove the three attributes from `make_expected_exaone4_1p2b_provider()`. The test still checks `rope_scaling=True` and `rope_scaling_factor=16.0`, the only llama3 RoPE values Megatron Core reads. Setting attributes that don't exist on the config is the phantom-field pattern AGENTS.md rules out for tests.\n\n# Verification\n\n- Bisected locally on CPU (Megatron Core 6e7e6ed4, Transformers 5.20, Transformer Engine stubbed; the test only builds and compares configs). The test passes at fc9b814a6^ and fails at fc9b814a6 and 20dd692f1 with the CI error. With this change it passes on current `main` (b35f75578).\n- `pre-commit run --all-files` passes.\n- Labeled `full-test-suite` so this PR runs L2. The launcher stops at the first failure (`-x`), so the failing nightly did not run the four EXAONE 4.5 and EXAONE MoE conversion tests in the same group. This PR's L2 run covers them.\n\n# GitHub Actions CI\n\nSee the [CI section](https://github.com/NVIDIA-NeMo/Megatron-Bridge/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md#-running-github-ci) in the Contributing doc for how to trigger the CI. A Nvidia developer will need to approve and trigger the CI for external contributors.\n\n# Before your PR is \"Ready for review\"\n\n**Pre checks**:\n\n- [x] Make sure you read and followed [Contributor guidelines](https://github.com/NVIDIA-NeMo/Megatron-Bridge/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] Did you write any new necessary tests?\n- [ ] Did you add or update any necessary documentation?\n- [ ] Does the PR affect components that are optional to install? (Ex: Numba, Pynini, Apex etc)\n  - [ ] Reviewer: Does the PR have correct import guards for all optional libraries?\n\n# Additional Information\n\n- Follow-up to #6401.\n",
